„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections–…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ3Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvNow, thou son of man, wilt thou judge, wilt thou judge the bloody city? yea, thou shalt shew her all her abominations.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸThen say thou, Thus saith the Lord GOD, The city sheddeth blood in the midst of it, that her time may come, and maketh idols against herself to defile herself.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚThou art become guilty in thy blood that thou hast shed; and hast defiled thyself in thine idols which thou hast made; and thou hast caused thy days to draw near, and art come even unto thy years: therefore have I made thee a reproach unto the heathen, and a mocking to all countries.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhThose that be near, and those that be far from thee, shall mock thee, which art infamous and much vexed.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSBehold, the princes of Israel, every one were in thee to their power to shed blood.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­In thee have they set light by father and mother: in the midst of thee have they dealt by oppression with the stranger: in thee have they vexed the fatherless and the widow.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCThou hast despised mine holy things, and hast profaned my sabbaths.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒIn thee are men that carry tales to shed blood: and in thee they eat upon the mountains: in the midst of thee they commit lewdness.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvIn thee have they discovered their fathers' nakedness: in thee have they humbled her that was set apart for pollution.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶And one hath committed abomination with his neighbour's wife; and another hath lewdly defiled his daughter in law; and another in thee hath humbled his sister, his father's daughter.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹In thee have they taken gifts to shed blood; thou hast taken usury and increase, and thou hast greedily gained of thy neighbours by extortion, and hast forgotten me, saith the Lord GOD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBehold, therefore I have smitten mine hand at thy dishonest gain which thou hast made, and at thy blood which hath been in the midst of thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰Can thine heart endure, or can thine hands be strong, in the days that I shall deal with thee? I the LORD have spoken it, and will do it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{And I will scatter thee among the heathen, and disperse thee in the countries, and will consume thy filthiness out of thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuAnd thou shalt take thine inheritance in thyself in the sight of the heathen, and thou shalt know that I am the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ.And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§Son of man, the house of Israel is to me become dross: all they are brass, and tin, and iron, and lead, in the midst of the furnace; they are even the dross of silver.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because ye are all become dross, behold, therefore I will gather you into the midst of Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙàAs they gather silver, and brass, and iron, and lead, and tin, into the midst of the furnace, to blow the fire upon it, to melt it; so will I gather you in mine anger and in my fury, and I will leave you there, and melt you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoYea, I will gather you, and blow upon you in the fire of my wrath, and ye shall be melted in the midst thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ As silver is melted in the midst of the furnace, so shall ye be melted in the midst thereof; and ye shall know that I the LORD have poured out my fury upon you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ.And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlSon of man, say unto her, Thou art the land that is not cleansed, nor rained upon in the day of indignation.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙãThere is a conspiracy of her prophets in the midst thereof, like a roaring lion ravening the prey; they have devoured souls; they have taken the treasure and precious things; they have made her many widows in the midst thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚHer priests have violated my law, and have profaned mine holy things: they have put no difference between the holy and profane, neither have they shewed difference between the unclean and the clean, and have hid their eyes from my sabbaths, and I am profaned among them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHer princes in the midst thereof are like wolves ravening the prey, to shed blood, and to destroy souls, to get dishonest gain.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥And her prophets have daubed them with untempered morter, seeing vanity, and divining lies unto them, saying, Thus saith the Lord GOD, when the LORD hath not spoken.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜The people of the land have used oppression, and exercised robbery, and have vexed the poor and needy: yea, they have oppressed the stranger wrongfully.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd I sought for a man among them, that should make up the hedge, and stand in the gap before me for the land, that I should not destroy it: but I found none.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®Therefore have I poured out mine indignation upon them; I have consumed them with the fire of my wrath: their own way have I recompensed upon their heads, saith the Lord GOD.¦layout ªlast_verse